1
00:04:21,818 --> 00:04:27,818
The most unusual triangle in the history of love: a boy, a girl, and a computer.

2
00:08:43,636 --> 00:08:49,636
Electric Dreams is a comedy, science fiction,
music film directed by Steve Barron.

3
00:13:05,454 --> 00:13:11,454
Miles buys himself a state-of-the-art computer that starts expressing
thoughts and emotions after having champagne spilled on it.

4
00:17:27,272 --> 00:17:33,272
Things start getting out of hand when both Miles and Edgar, the
computer, fall in love with Madeline, an attractive neighbor.

5
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:55,090
Miles Harding, played by Lenny Von Dohlen.

6
00:26:10,909 --> 00:26:16,909
Madeline Robistat, played by Virginia Madsen.

7
00:30:32,727 --> 00:30:38,727
Bill, played by Maxwell Caulfield.

8
00:34:54,545 --> 00:35:00,545
Edgar (voice), played by Bud Cort.

9
00:39:16,363 --> 00:39:22,363
Mr. Ryley, played by Don Fellows.

10
00:43:38,181 --> 00:43:44,181
Frank, played by Alan Polonsky.

11
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Electric Dreams is a 1984 science fiction romantic comedy film directed by Steve Barron
(in his feature film directorial debut) and written by Rusty Lemorande.

12
00:52:21,818 --> 00:52:27,818
The film is set in San Francisco, focusing on a love triangle between an architect (Lenny Von Dohlen), a
cellist (Virginia Madsen), and a personal computer named Edgar (Bud Cort) that gains sentience.

13
00:56:43,636 --> 00:56:49,636
The film was produced by Virgin Films, and is noted for its new wave soundtrack and
visual style, reflecting Barron's background as a music video director.

14
01:01:05,454 --> 01:01:11,454
The score was composed by Giorgio Moroder, and the soundtrack
features the hit single "Together in Electric Dreams".

15
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
The narrative repeatedly has been cited as a modern retelling of the classic 1897 French play
Cyrano de Bergerac, exploring the intersection of human emotion and technology.

16
01:09:49,090 --> 01:09:55,090
The film's premise reflected the cultural zeitgeist of the early 1980s, and its production coincided with Time magazine naming the
personal computer its "Machine of the Year" for 1982, signaling the technology's integration into domestic life.

17
01:14:10,909 --> 01:14:16,909
Electric Dreams was released in the United States by MGM/UA Entertainment Co.

18
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
on July 20, 1984, and in the United Kingdom by
20th Century Fox on August 17, 1984.

19
01:22:54,545 --> 01:23:00,545
It was a commercial disappointment and received mixed reviews from critics upon release, but
has since developed a cult following and drawn comparisons to the 2013 film Her.

20
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
The film explores themes of computer, architect, cello.

21
01:31:38,181 --> 01:31:44,181
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
